{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_platform_analysis_execution_pipeline", "label": "Execution Pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "1 / 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Persisted runs, error classification, staged self-healing with deterministic verification, auto-adopt policy, versioned rollback; positioned as ahead of Browse AI's 'robots that adapt' in transparency."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_self_healing", "label": "Self-healing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2 / 8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Empty-result detection, snapshot-verified fixes, confidence-gated auto-adopt, one-click manual adopt, full audit trail in run_repairs; a competitive differentiator."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_api_discovery", "label": "API Discovery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2 / 8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Passively capture XHR/fetch, propose the site's underlying JSON API, replay-verify, and emit an EXTRACT_API step instead of scraping the DOM; a differentiator neither competitor ships."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_code_export", "label": "Code Export (Puppeteer)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2 / 8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Download a standalone Puppeteer script plus tailored README; the 'no lock-in' differentiator (your scraper exports as runnable code)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_quick_scrape_wizard", "label": "Quick Scrape Wizard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-button guided list scraping chaining navigate -> container detection -> AI field proposal -> pagination into one linear flow, then hands finished steps to the editor (QuickScrapeWizard.jsx)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_dashboard", "label": "Dashboard Home", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Post-login landing with per-workflow status cards, a needs-attention inbox with AI summaries, schedule/next-run, and change indicators (Dashboard.jsx)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_condition_builder", "label": "No-code Condition Builder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "5.1 / 6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Field/operator/value dropdowns compiling to JS with 'edit as code' preserved, wired for IF / WHILE expressions (ConditionBuilder.jsx)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_scheduling", "label": "Scheduling (interval + time-of-day)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2 / 5.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Partial: interval + time-of-day anchor (ScheduleEditor.jsx); no cron and no weekday selection yet."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_dataset_view", "label": "Cross-run Dataset View", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rows unioned and de-duplicated across a workflow's retained successful runs with first/last-seen and times-seen; computed on read, so it works retroactively with no new storage (dataset.service.js, DatasetPanel.jsx)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_excel_export", "label": "Excel (.xlsx) Export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.6.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "xlsx workbook with one worksheet per output list from run results and datasets; JSON/CSV also supported (resultsXlsx.js)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_csv_export", "label": "CSV Export (shared header-union serialiser)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "3.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single header-union serialiser (resultsExport.js) takes headers from the union of all rows, not row 0 only, so columns missing from the first row are not dropped; the frontend shares it with a parity test that fails the build if the two ever drift. Powers both the in-app download and GET /v1/runs/:id/data?format=csv."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_change_monitoring", "label": "Change Monitoring & Alerts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-workflow 'watch for changes': after each successful run, row-level diff (add/remove/change) vs the previous run, keyed the same way the dataset view dedupes; store the summary on the run and fire run.changed through the webhook dispatcher. Change feed on dashboard, run history, and monitor editor. Email delivery still future (changeDiff.service.js, changeMonitor.service.js, MonitorEditor.jsx)."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_webhooks", "label": "Webhooks (dispatcher + events)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2 / 5.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dispatcher + API + three events (run.completed / run.failed / run.changed); partial because there is still no UI to register/manage them."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_run_history_versioning", "label": "Run History & Versioning", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every run pins the executed version; one-click rollback; logs, repairs, and AI summaries retained."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_pagination_handling", "label": "Pagination Handling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three native containers (scroll/button/URL) plus a two-phase detector (static DOM scan + empirical scroll test) with confidence scores."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_ai_field_suggestion", "label": "AI Field Suggestion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LLM proposal + live-DOM verification + heuristic fallback + intent-rescue merging; degrades gracefully with no API key."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_public_rest_api", "label": "Public REST API (feature inventory)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/v1 with hashed API keys, idempotency, cursor pagination, rate limits, quotas, signed webhooks, and a consistent error shape; matches the competitor API concept."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_roadmap", "label": "Prioritized Roadmap (P0-P3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "P0 correctness & production hygiene and P1 non-technical breakthrough are done; P2 competitive parity mostly done; P3 power-user polish open. Document doubles as the roadmap, marked shipped / partial / open."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_template_gallery", "label": "Template Gallery (open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ship 6-10 saved workflows as JSON seeds plus a 'start from template' flow; cheap once workflow export/import exists because templates are the same JSON."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_workflow_export_import", "label": "Workflow Export/Import/Duplicate (open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "5.2.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Needed for backup, sharing, start-from-a-copy, and as the substrate for templates."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_webhook_management_ui", "label": "Webhook Management UI (open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "5.2.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Today only POST /v1/webhooks registers one; there is no UI to list/manage endpoints."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_google_sheets_delivery", "label": "Google Sheets Delivery (open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.6.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Live push to Sheets still open; the webhook-dispatcher path is the right attachment point. Excel covers the offline case."}, {"id": "docs_platform_analysis_bulk_input_lists", "label": "Bulk Input Lists (open)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PLATFORM_ANALYSIS.md", "source_location": "6.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": 